      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is absolutely true that if the thing that gave life its color is gone, the rest of it can feel like just static. That heavy feeling you're describing isn't a weakness; it's the weight of a massive, undeniable loss. Instead of trying to force yourself to \"be,\" maybe you can focus on the quiet, small acts that require the least effort—the simple, undeniable fact of your own breathing. Sometimes, the only real point left is the act of simply existing through the next minute.",
